<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mario Lago</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mario Lago was an Italian diplomat and governor of the Italian Islands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese">Dodecanese</a>, from 1922 to 1936. He invested in roads, farming, archaeology and public buildings, restoring the Palace of the Grand Master in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> and sponsoring Italian rationalist architecture. His relatively mild rule was followed by harsher Italianisation under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-maria-de-vecchi">Cesare Maria De Vecchi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mario-lago.jpg" alt="Mario Lago" width="287" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Genthe, Arnold, 1869-1942, photographer · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_photograph_of_Mario_Rodi_Lago.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
